.TH INTRO 3
.SH NAME
intro \- introduction to the library functions
.SH DESCRIPTION
This section describes the functions of the libraries that
.BR cc (1)
links with programs. They are kept in /usr/lib/cc:
.TP 16
.B libc.a
The C library: standard input and output, strings, conversions,
memory, time, and the system calls. Every program is linked with it.
.TP
.B libm.a
The math library: exp, log, pow, sqrt, the trigonometric and hyperbolic
functions, floor, ceil, fmod and hypot. A program that uses it is linked
with
.BR \-lm ,
written after the files that use it:
.RS
.PP
.nf
	cc \-o prog prog.c \-lm
.fi
.RE
.TP 16
.B libtermcap.a
The terminal capability library,
.BR termcap (3).
Link with
.BR \-ltermcap .
.PP
The headers in /usr/include declare the functions, and define the
types and constants they use; the page of each function names its
header. In C without function prototypes, a function that returns
anything but an int must be declared before it is called, or its value
is taken to be an int: include the header, or declare the function, as
in
.BR "double atof();" .
.PP
The pages, by subject:
.TP 16
input, output
stdio(3), fopen(3), fclose(3), getc(3), gets(3), putc(3), puts(3),
printf(3), scanf(3), fread(3), fseek(3), ungetc(3), ferror(3),
setbuf(3)
.TP
strings
string(3), memory(3), ctype(3)
.TP
numbers
atof(3), ecvt(3), abs(3), frexp(3)
.TP
mathematics
exp(3), trig(3), sinh(3), floor(3), hypot(3), matherr(3)
.TP
memory
malloc(3)
.TP
time
ctime(3), sleep(3)
.TP
errors
perror(3), abort(3), setjmp(3)
.TP
the system
getenv(3), system(3), isatty(3), rename(3), setlocale(3)
.TP
terminals
termcap(3)
.PP
.B man \-k
finds a function by a word of its description.
.SH FILES
.TP 26
/usr/lib/cc/libc.a
the C library
.TP
/usr/lib/cc/libm.a
the math library
.TP
/usr/lib/cc/libtermcap.a
the terminal capability library
.TP
/usr/include
the headers
.SH SEE ALSO
cc(1), intro(1), man(1), nm(1)
.SH HISTORY
In Version 7 AT&T UNIX, as here, the math functions were in a library
of their own, linked with \-lm. The page of each function tells where
it first appeared.
